HST Office: the status bar of a document window in the HST look (the frame coat's StatusBar part).

- Only colours and shapes change: the bar's height, the items' widths and their click areas are exactly as
  without the coat (owner decision D9). The look applies to the bar of a document window (its parent is
  the frame's work window) while org.openoffice.Office.HSTAppearance/FrameCoat/StatusBar and the coat are
  on, and never in high contrast; the bars of dialogs keep the platform's look.
- StatusBar (vcl/source/window/status.cxx, thin hooks): the frame surface instead of the native
  background, item text in the text colour (the bar keeps its font, which sizes the bar and its items), a
  thin divider of the frame divider colour, inset at both ends, instead of the 3D separator, the frame
  divider along the top edge, and a rounded hover behind every item that does something on a single click
  in Writer, Sheets and Slides (saved state, signature, language, zoom percentage; page number, word
  count, accessibility check, page style, insert mode, selection mode; sheet position, page style,
  AutoCalculate; slide number, slide layout, fit slide), not behind an item whose text is empty, repainted
  only when the item under the mouse changes and cleared when the items move. A paint redraws only the
  items (and their dividers) in the invalidated area, so a word count update repaints that item alone, not
  the zoom slider beside it.
- The zoom slider (svx/source/stbctrls/zoomsliderctrl.cxx): a groove of the scroll-track colour outlined
  with the frame divider, short marks for the snapping points, a longer 100 % mark in the text colour and
  a narrow upright accent pill for the thumb, all vector shapes at the window's scale. The decrease and
  increase buttons stay the icon theme's images, where the control takes their clicks; their HST glyphs
  come with the icon set.
- The drawing is in vcl/source/hst/coat/coat-statusbar.cxx behind <vcl/hst/statusbarcoat.hxx>: flat fills
  only, no gradient, no bitmap of its own.
- CppunitTest_vcl_hst_statusbar_coat: the frame colours light and dark, the thin dividers, the hover on
  clickable items only and not on empty ones, the list of clickable commands, the unchanged height and
  item rectangles, the platform look in high contrast, for a dialog's bar and with the part switched off,
  the zoom slider's shapes and thumb at 50/100/200 %, and no more item repaints with the coat than without
  over 1,000 text updates.

